# Check numbers vs internal references

Do not conflate these fields.

| Concept | Frontend / UI | Backend / API | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Paper check number | Label: **Check number** / **Check #**. Portal model: `checkNumber`. | `paymentReference` (legacy `checkNumber` dual-read/write) | Keep as a **string**. Preserve leading zeros. Never coerce with `Number()`. |
| Internal transaction reference | Label: **Internal reference** / **Internal ref #**. Portal model: `refNumber`. | `refNumber` | EMSYS internal id. Not the paper check number. |

## Rules

- **UI always says “Check number.”** Never surface the backend name `paymentReference` in labels or column titles.
- Map API `paymentReference` → portal `checkNumber` on read (legacy `checkNumber` fallback). On write, dual-send `paymentReference` + legacy `checkNumber` with the same string value.
- When journals generate outstanding checks, that string carries through supported reference fields so leading zeros survive.
- Checks table **Check #** renders portal `checkNumber` (already normalized from `paymentReference`). **Internal ref #** renders `refNumber` only.
- Do not use `refNumber` as a fallback when resolving a paper check number.
- `external_reference_number` is a separate optional payment reference (e.g. Zelle) — not the check number.
